    {
      "id": "c9517cc7-2d84-4b68-8493-75b61e23f9ea",
      "name": "darkminimal",
      "html": "<!DOCTYPE html>\n<html lang=\"en\">\n<head>\n<meta charset=\"UTF-8\">\n<meta name=\"viewport\" content=\"width=device-width, initial-scale=1.0\">\n<title>Dark Minimal \u2014 Wireframe</title>\n<style>\n  *,*::before,*::after{box-sizing:border-box;margin:0;padding:0}\n  body{font-family:Georgia,serif;background:#ffffff;color:#000000}\n  .page{max-width:1080px;margin:0 auto;min-height:1080px;background:#ffffff;display:grid;grid-template-columns:210px 1fr;align-content:center}\n  .b{background:#ffffff;border:1px solid #000000;border-radius:3px;display:flex;align-items:center;justify-content:center;font-family:monospace;font-size:30px;color:#000000;letter-spacing:.04em;overflow:hidden;min-width:120px;min-height:80px}\n  .side{padding:49px 20px;display:flex;flex-direction:column;gap:15px}\n  /* Was a horizontal icon+label row \u2014 at 3x text size, two 120px-floor boxes\n     side by side no longer fit the 210px sidebar column's ~170px content\n     width, so this stacks icon above label instead of narrowing the boxes\n     below their readable-text floor or widening the grid column (which\n     would change the page's internal proportions). */\n  .si{display:flex;flex-direction:column;align-items:flex-start;gap:11px;margin-top:19px}\n  .main{padding:65px 40px;position:relative;display:flex;flex-direction:column;gap:65px}\n  .sec{display:flex;align-items:center;justify-content:space-between;gap:20px}\n</style>\n</head>\n<body>\n<!-- 210px sidebar column previously carried container-1, but it and its\n     children use the same .b/.si styling as ordinary page content \u2014 no\n     visual boundary of its own \u2014 so container-1 was removed and all boxes\n     are now plain leaves. No header or footer tag/bar exists in this file.\n     The two remaining .b.red icon boxes (originally image-1/2/3 before the\n     box-N relabel, one dropped in the reference trim) are now stacked above\n     their label (see .si comment above) rather than beside it. 0 containers\n     in this file. -->\n<div class=\"page\">\n  <aside class=\"side\">\n    <div class=\"si\"><div class=\"b red\" style=\"width:120px;height:42px\">box-1</div><div class=\"b\" style=\"width:90%\">box-2</div></div>\n    <div class=\"b\" style=\"height:14px;width:90%\">box-3</div>\n    <div class=\"b\" style=\"height:14px;width:70%\">box-4</div>\n    <div class=\"si\"><div class=\"b red\" style=\"width:120px;height:42px\">box-5</div><div class=\"b\" style=\"width:90%\">box-6</div></div>\n    <div class=\"b\" style=\"height:14px;width:70%\">box-7</div>\n    <div class=\"b\" style=\"height:14px;width:80%\">box-8</div>\n  </aside>\n  <main class=\"main\">\n    <div class=\"b\" style=\"width:300px;height:380px\">box-9</div>\n    <div class=\"b\" style=\"height:40px;width:70%\">box-10</div>\n    <div class=\"sec\"><div class=\"b\" style=\"height:34px;width:46%\">box-11</div><div class=\"b faint\" style=\"width:220px;height:103px\">box-12</div></div>\n    <div class=\"sec\"><div class=\"b\" style=\"height:95px;width:50%\">box-13</div><div class=\"b faint\" style=\"width:280px;height:103px\">box-14</div></div>\n  </main>\n</div>\n</body>\n</html>\n"
    },
    {
      "id": "58f6757d-6c99-4e7e-ba80-f16c93699661",
      "name": "stickynotes",
      "html": "<!DOCTYPE html>\n<html lang=\"en\">\n<head>\n<meta charset=\"UTF-8\">\n<meta name=\"viewport\" content=\"width=device-width, initial-scale=1.0\">\n<title>Sticky Notes \u2014 Wireframe</title>\n<style>\n  *,*::before,*::after{box-sizing:border-box;margin:0;padding:0}\n  body{font-family:Georgia,serif;background:#ffffff;color:#000000}\n  .page{max-width:1080px;margin:0 auto;min-height:1080px;background:#ffffff;display:flex;flex-direction:column;justify-content:center}\n  .b{background:#ffffff;border:1px solid #000000;border-radius:3px;display:flex;align-items:center;justify-content:center;font-family:monospace;font-size:30px;color:#000000;letter-spacing:.04em;overflow:hidden;min-width:120px;min-height:65px}\n  /* box-5 (rightmost, hnav is margin-left:auto so it hugs the right edge)\n     shares the top-right corner with the container-1 badge \u2014 was\n     align-items:center in a fixed 66px bar, which doesn't push content\n     below the badge at any height. Top-aligned with matching top padding\n     instead, same fix as .panel/.card. */\n  header{background:#ffffff;display:flex;align-items:flex-start;gap:18px;padding:68px 30px 25px;border:1px dashed #000000}\n  .hnav{display:flex;gap:12px;margin-left:auto}\n  .intro{display:flex;gap:18px;padding:37px 30px 16px;align-items:flex-start}\n  .cards{display:flex;gap:16px;padding:12px 30px 47px;align-items:flex-start}\n  .card{flex:1;background:#ffffff;border:1px dashed #000000;padding:68px 14px 25px;display:flex;flex-direction:column;gap:16px;position:relative}\n  .col{display:flex;flex-direction:column;gap:14px}\n  .ctnr{position:relative}\n  .ctag{position:absolute;top:4px;right:4px;z-index:5;color:#fff;font-family:monospace;font-size:24px;letter-spacing:.03em;padding:3px 6px;border-radius:2px;pointer-events:none}\n</style>\n</head>\n<body>\n<div class=\"page\">\n  <!-- Genuine <header> tag: header container. No footer or sidebar exists\n       in this single-column layout, so none is forced (same as steel's\n       missing footer). Each .card below has a real background (#f1ecdc)\n       + border, distinct from the page background (#c9bfa6) \u2014 a genuine\n       visual boundary \u2014 so each gets its own container (container-2/3,\n       left to right). -->\n  <header class=\"ctnr\">\n    <span class=\"ctag\">container-1</span>\n    <div class=\"b\" style=\"width:80px;height:20px\">box-1</div>\n    <div class=\"b\" style=\"width:220px;height:26px\">box-2</div>\n    <div class=\"hnav\">\n      <div class=\"b\" style=\"width:120px;height:22px\">box-3</div>\n      <div class=\"b\" style=\"width:90px;height:22px\">box-4</div>\n      <div class=\"b\" style=\"width:100px;height:22px\">box-5</div>\n    </div>\n  </header>\n\n  <div class=\"intro\">\n    <div class=\"b\" style=\"width:120px;height:186px\">box-6</div>\n    <div class=\"col\" style=\"width:300px\">\n      <div class=\"b\" style=\"height:40px\">box-7</div>\n      <div style=\"display:flex;gap:8px\"><div class=\"b\" style=\"width:90px;height:18px\">box-8</div><div class=\"b\" style=\"width:70px;height:18px\">box-9</div></div>\n    </div>\n  </div>\n\n  <div class=\"cards\">\n    <div class=\"card\">\n      <span class=\"ctag\">container-2</span>\n      <div class=\"b\" style=\"height:20px;width:88%\">box-10</div>\n      <div class=\"b\" style=\"height:186px\">box-11</div>\n      <div class=\"b\" style=\"height:124px\">box-12</div>\n    </div>\n    <div class=\"card\">\n      <span class=\"ctag\">container-3</span>\n      <div class=\"b\" style=\"height:20px;width:80%\">box-13</div>\n      <div class=\"b\" style=\"height:233px\">box-14</div>\n      <div class=\"b\" style=\"height:109px\">box-15</div>\n    </div>\n  </div>\n</div>\n</body>\n</html>\n"
    },
    {
      "id": "c61427b9-dc32-418f-bb16-4d4ea009349d",
      "name": "midcentury",
      "html": "<!DOCTYPE html>\n<html lang=\"en\">\n<head>\n<meta charset=\"UTF-8\">\n<meta name=\"viewport\" content=\"width=device-width, initial-scale=1.0\">\n<title>Mid Century \u2014 Wireframe</title>\n<style>\n  *,*::before,*::after{box-sizing:border-box;margin:0;padding:0}\n  body{font-family:Georgia,serif;background:#ffffff;color:#ffffff}\n  .page{max-width:1080px;margin:0 auto;background:#ffffff;min-height:1080px;display:flex;flex-direction:column;justify-content:center}\n  .b{background:#ffffff;border:1px solid #000000;border-radius:3px;display:flex;align-items:center;justify-content:center;font-family:monospace;font-size:30px;color:#000000;letter-spacing:.04em;overflow:hidden;min-width:120px;min-height:55px}\n  /* hnav (justify-content:flex-end) hugs the right edge, same corner as the\n     container-1 badge \u2014 was align-items:center in a fixed 78px bar, which\n     doesn't clear the badge at any height. Top-aligned with matching top\n     padding instead, same fix as .card/.panel/header (stickynotes). */\n  header{background:#ffffff;border:1px dashed #000000;display:flex;align-items:flex-start;justify-content:space-between;padding:57px 30px 21px}\n  .htitles{display:flex;flex-direction:column;gap:9px}\n  .hnav{display:flex;gap:8px;flex-wrap:wrap;width:520px;justify-content:flex-end}\n  .cards{display:flex;gap:18px;padding:34px 30px}\n  .cards .b{flex:1;height:241px}\n  .body{display:grid;grid-template-columns:230px 1fr;gap:26px;padding:0 30px 39px}\n  .col{display:flex;flex-direction:column;gap:16px}\n  .foot{background:#ffffff;border:1px dashed #000000;display:flex;gap:14px;padding:21px 30px;flex-wrap:wrap}\n  .ctnr{position:relative}\n  .ctag{position:absolute;top:4px;right:4px;z-index:5;background:rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.55);color:#000000;font-family:monospace;font-size:24px;letter-spacing:.03em;padding:3px 6px;border-radius:2px;pointer-events:none}\n</style>\n</head>\n<body>\n<div class=\"page\">\n  <!-- Genuine <header> tag, full-width bar at the top: header container. -->\n  <header class=\"ctnr\">\n    <span class=\"ctag\">container-1</span>\n    <div class=\"htitles\">\n      <div class=\"b\" style=\"width:220px;height:26px\">box-1</div>\n    </div>\n    <div class=\"hnav\">\n      <div class=\"b\" style=\"width:120px;height:14px\">box-2</div>\n      <div class=\"b\" style=\"width:90px;height:14px\">box-3</div>\n      <div class=\"b\" style=\"width:110px;height:14px\">box-4</div>\n    </div>\n  </header>\n\n  <div class=\"cards\">\n    <div class=\"b\">box-5</div>\n    <div class=\"b\">box-6</div>\n    <div class=\"b\">box-7</div>\n  </div>\n\n  <div class=\"body\">\n    <!-- Left column: narrow (230px), structurally distinct from the wide\n         (1fr) right column, but it and its children (box-8/9/10) use the\n         same .b styling as ordinary page content \u2014 no visual boundary of\n         its own \u2014 so container-2 was removed and its boxes are now plain\n         leaves. -->\n    <div class=\"col\">\n      <div class=\"b\" style=\"height:22px;width:80%\">box-8</div>\n      <div class=\"b\" style=\"height:195px\">box-9</div>\n      <div class=\"b\" style=\"height:117px\">box-10</div>\n    </div>\n    <div class=\"col\">\n      <div class=\"b\" style=\"height:24px;width:50%\">box-11</div>\n      <div class=\"b\" style=\"height:91px\">box-12</div>\n      <div class=\"b\" style=\"height:117px\">box-13</div>\n    </div>\n  </div>\n\n  <!-- Bottom-most full-width bar: footer container (no <footer> tag, but\n       passes the literal \"bottom-most full-width bar\" test). -->\n  <div class=\"foot ctnr\">\n    <span class=\"ctag\">container-2</span>\n    <div class=\"b\" style=\"width:70px;height:16px\">box-14</div>\n    <div class=\"b\" style=\"width:60px;height:16px\">box-15</div>\n  </div>\n</div>\n</body>\n</html>\n"
    },
    {
      "id": "3d208f14-067a-419e-ab6a-5d0badf2ba12",
      "name": "steel",
      "html": "<!DOCTYPE html>\n<html lang=\"en\">\n<head>\n<meta charset=\"UTF-8\">\n<meta name=\"viewport\" content=\"width=device-width, initial-scale=1.0\">\n<title>Steel \u2014 Wireframe</title>\n<style>\n  *,*::before,*::after{box-sizing:border-box;margin:0;padding:0}\n  body{font-family:Georgia,serif;background:#ffffff;color:#000000}\n  .page{max-width:1080px;margin:0 auto;min-height:1080px;background:#ffffff;display:flex;flex-direction:column;justify-content:center}\n  .b{background:#ffffff;border:1px solid #000000;border-radius:2px;display:flex;align-items:center;justify-content:center;font-family:monospace;font-size:30px;color:#000000;letter-spacing:.04em;overflow:hidden;min-width:120px;min-height:76px}\n  /* Was position:absolute against .page \u2014 that anchored it to the page's\n     TOP regardless of where the (now vertically centered) .grid content\n     ends up, leaving it stranded far from the grid. In-flow with matching\n     margin instead, so it moves together with .grid as one centered unit. */\n  .banner-slot{margin:32px 0 0 40px;width:360px;height:34px}\n  .grid{display:grid;grid-template-columns:220px 1fr 200px;gap:26px;padding:0 30px 72px}\n  .panel{background:#ffffff;padding:79px 14px 29px;display:flex;flex-direction:column;gap:14px;margin-bottom:32px;position:relative}\n  .col{display:flex;flex-direction:column;gap:29px}\n  .ctnr{position:relative}\n  .ctag{position:absolute;top:4px;right:4px;z-index:5;background:#ffffff;color:#ffffff;font-family:monospace;font-size:24px;letter-spacing:.03em;padding:3px 6px;border-radius:2px;pointer-events:none}\n</style>\n</head>\n<body>\n<div class=\"page\">\n  <!-- Skewed banner above the grid: 367px wide inside a 1080px page (~34%),\n       fails the header literal-identification test (no <header> tag, not\n       full-width) \u2014 kept as a plain leaf box, not wrapped in a container. -->\n  <div class=\"b banner-slot\">box-1</div>\n  <div class=\"grid\">\n    <!-- Left sidebar column (220px): narrow layout wrapper, but the <aside>\n         itself has no background of its own \u2014 same page background as the\n         grid \u2014 so it is not a container. Each .panel inside DOES have a\n         real background (#2b323c) distinct from the page (#171b21), so\n         each panel gets its own container instead (container-1/2/3, top to\n         bottom). -->\n    <aside class=\"col\">\n      <div class=\"panel\">\n        <span class=\"ctag\">container-1</span>\n        <div class=\"b y\" style=\"height:16px;width:80%\">box-2</div>\n        <div class=\"b\" style=\"height:14px;width:90%\">box-3</div>\n        <div class=\"b\" style=\"height:14px;width:70%\">box-4</div>\n      </div>\n      <div class=\"panel\">\n        <span class=\"ctag\">container-2</span>\n        <div class=\"b y\" style=\"height:15px;width:55%\">box-5</div>\n        <div class=\"b\" style=\"height:13px;width:75%\">box-6</div>\n        <div class=\"b\" style=\"height:13px;width:60%\">box-7</div>\n      </div>\n    </aside>\n    <!-- Centre <main> column: same reasoning \u2014 the column wrapper has no\n         background of its own, but the remaining .panel does, so it gets\n         its own container (container-3). -->\n    <main class=\"col\">\n      <div class=\"panel\"><span class=\"ctag\">container-3</span><div class=\"b y\" style=\"height:18px;width:46%\">box-8</div><div class=\"b\" style=\"height:180px\">box-9</div></div>\n    </main>\n    <!-- Right sidebar column (200px): same reasoning as the left sidebar\n         above \u2014 the <aside> wrapper is not a container, but each .panel is\n         (container-4/5, top to bottom). -->\n    <aside class=\"col\">\n      <div class=\"panel\"><span class=\"ctag\">container-4</span><div class=\"b y\" style=\"height:16px;width:90%\">box-10</div><div class=\"b\" style=\"height:288px\">box-11</div></div>\n      <div class=\"panel\"><span class=\"ctag\">container-5</span><div class=\"b\" style=\"height:30px;width:80%\">box-12</div><div class=\"b\" style=\"height:14px;width:50%\">box-13</div></div>\n    </aside>\n  </div>\n</div>\n</body>\n</html>\n"
    },
    {
      "id": "d7a2d7fc-b8a8-4209-bced-f6ddc07a4887",
      "name": "retro",
      "html": "<!DOCTYPE html>\n<html lang=\"en\">\n<head>\n<meta charset=\"UTF-8\">\n<meta name=\"viewport\" content=\"width=device-width, initial-scale=1.0\">\n<title>Retro \u2014 Wireframe</title>\n<style>\n  *,*::before,*::after{box-sizing:border-box;margin:0;padding:0}\n  body{font-family:'Comic Sans MS',Georgia,serif;background:#ffffff;color:#000000}\n  .page{max-width:1080px;margin:0 auto;min-height:1080px;background:#ffffff;padding:31px 0;display:flex;flex-direction:column;justify-content:center}\n  .col{width:520px;margin:0 auto;background:#ffffff;padding:31px 22px;display:flex;flex-direction:column;gap:14px;align-items:center}\n  .b{background:#ffffff;border:1px solid #000000;border-radius:3px;display:flex;align-items:center;justify-content:center;font-family:monospace;font-size:30px;color:#000000;letter-spacing:.04em;overflow:hidden;min-width:120px;min-height:71px}\n  .row{display:flex;gap:10px;justify-content:center;flex-wrap:wrap}\n  .full{width:100%}\n  .ctnr{position:relative}\n  .ctag{position:absolute;top:4px;right:4px;z-index:5;color:#000000;font-family:monospace;font-size:24px;letter-spacing:.03em;padding:3px 6px;border-radius:2px;pointer-events:none}\n</style>\n</head>\n<body>\n<!-- Only one container in this file: it's a single narrow (520px, ~48% of\n     the 1080px page) centered column \u2014 the topmost banner (text-1, now\n     box-1) fails the literal full-page-width test for a header, same\n     reasoning as steel's rejected banner, and there is no side column\n     structurally distinct from a main area, so no sidebar either. The\n     nested .col below (box-9 through box-13) DOES have a genuine visual\n     boundary \u2014 solid fill distinct from the page background \u2014 so it\n     becomes container-1. Every other box in this file (box-1 through\n     box-8) stays plain. All box-level accent classes (rainbow/yellow/\n     black/magenta/dashed) were removed corpus-wide for color consistency\n     \u2014 every box is now the same white fill regardless of role. -->\n<div class=\"page\">\n  <div class=\"col\">\n    <div class=\"b full\" style=\"height:34px\">box-1</div>\n    <div class=\"b full\" style=\"height:18px;width:70%\">box-2</div>\n    <div class=\"row full\">\n      <div class=\"b\" style=\"width:130px;height:75px\">box-3</div>\n      <div class=\"b\" style=\"height:75px;flex:1\">box-4</div>\n    </div>\n    <div class=\"row\"><div class=\"b\" style=\"width:40px;height:34px\">box-5</div><div class=\"b\" style=\"width:60px;height:34px\">box-6</div><div class=\"b\" style=\"width:40px;height:34px\">box-7</div></div>\n    <div class=\"b full\" style=\"height:20px;width:50%\">box-8</div>\n    <div class=\"col ctnr\" style=\"width:90%;gap:10px;padding:75px 22px 24px; border:1px dashed #000000\">\n      <span class=\"ctag\">container-1</span>\n      <div class=\"b full\" style=\"height:14px;width:70%\">box-9</div>\n      <div class=\"b full\" style=\"height:14px;width:55%\">box-10</div>\n      <div class=\"b full\" style=\"height:14px;width:65%\">box-11</div>\n      <div class=\"b full\" style=\"height:14px;width:60%\">box-12</div>\n      <div class=\"b full\" style=\"height:14px;width:50%\">box-13</div>\n    </div>\n  </div>\n</div>\n</body>\n</html>\n"
    }
  ]
}